is flexibility gave baker the ability  to play with the weight of theron's  lashline with the addition of fake  eyelids this transformed her eyes  according to makeup artist kazuhiro from  deep socketed to more hooded  to get a deeper shade of blue to match  kelly's eyes theron wore colored contact  lenses and to match what the makeup team  described as kelly's heart-shaped face  the team lowered theron's wig thus  lowering her hairline  hiro also created some traditional  prosthetics as well like an upturned  nose tip an angular jaw and chin pieces  actor gary oldman looks nothing like  winston churchill so when the actor was  cast to play churchill in darkest hour  makeup artist kazuhiro had to cover  oldman in nearly half his body weight  worth of special effects makeup  they did about three to five makeup  tests matching various silicone  prostheses to see what was crucial and  what wasn't hiro realized he could cover  oldman's cheeks jowls neck chin and nose  but oldman's eyes mouth and forehead  were important for emphasizing  expressions and emotions so hiro  intentionally left out some of  churchill's physical features like  discarding the piece for churchill's  real-life forehead scar that's why you  can see oldman's real forehead creases  emote as much as his mouth the team made  up for this diversion from the truth by  nailing details the viewer might not  even think of as essential  like giving the prosthetic pieces pink  and blotchy tones to match the leader's  skin  in the end even without the scar darkest  hour created a convincing churchill  leading to oscar wins for both oldman  and hiro  as seen in itanya visual effects can be  just as crucial to an actor's  transformation as makeup and training  margot robbie trained for five months to  skate like tonya harding but there were  multiple moves too difficult for a  non-olympic athlete and since harding's  skating routines are just as famous as  her public persona the film had to get  the moves exactly right so the team used  two vfx methods to seamlessly combine  robbie's training with her stunt doubles  for the first method a stunt double  would skate with an orange tennis ball  on her head her face would be swapped  out for robbie's  the second method was full head  replacement they 3d scanned robbie's  face to get a full range of her skin  texture and expressions in order to  build a digital model head replacement  was useful for complex shots like this  one which was actually three shots  stitched together because of this  careful work behind the scenes you'll  never be able to tell what part of the  shot is robbie and what part is a double  instead you can just focus on how robbie  imitated all of harding's mannerisms  from putting her hand over her face when  she's upset to raising her arms in a  moment of triumph  in rocketman the first step to  transforming taryn edgerton into elton  john was nailing the costumes especially  when edgerton was performing  after all jon himself said he doesn't  feel like the elton john until he  chooses his outfit for a show so costume  designer julian day closely modeled  edgerton's looks after john's real  outfits  this included designing 50 pairs of  glasses and 50 pairs of shoes one of  which was covered in real swarovski  crystals and while edgerton already knew  how to sing playing an instrument in  elton john's legendary style is a whole  other skill  edgerton spent six weeks training with  piano coach michael l roberts according  to roberts a piano is hard to perform at  since you can't move around with it like  you would with a guitar so edgerton  focused on the unique parts of john's  playing style such as how he leans into  his mic and sometimes plays with his  feet  roberts and edgerton also studied john's  musical influences like blues and boogie  woogie to get the right style of finger  placement  because of that physicality it really  felt like you were watching elton john  play  [Music]  you
 

